message: "If you use the software certifiers, please cite this software release. Code is BSD-3-Clause; original data and documentation are CC BY 4.0 as described in the repository licensing files."
title: "Certified lower bounds for unit-square Riesz 2-polarization"
type: software
version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kishimoto"
    given-names: "Satoshi"
abstract: "Exact-rational branch-and-bound certificates for fixed configurations in Erich Friedman's unit-square minimum-light-intensity problem (Riesz s=2 polarization). This corrective patch release rounds 18 published rigorous upper-witness decimals, and the interval widths that follow from them, outward instead of to nearest, so that each is an upper bound; it clarifies the descriptive provenance prose of n=15 and n=16; and it strengthens verification, replay validation, and frozen-corpus integrity checking. The 44 certified lower bounds, the exact finite-decimal configurations, the 88 exact certifier sources, and the preserved mathematical replay evidence are unchanged from v1.0.1."
keywords:
  - Riesz polarization
  - minimum light intensity
  - geometric optimization
  - exact rational arithmetic
  - branch and bound
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/Driedsandwich/square-riesz-polarization-certificates"
url: "https://github.com/Driedsandwich/square-riesz-polarization-certificates/releases/tag/v1.0.2"
